    <!-- S6213: variable matches a restricted identifier. Every occurrence is a  -->
    <!-- variable named "record" in the Kafka producer/consumer code and its     -->
    <!-- tests, as in "for (ConsumerRecord<Bytes, Bytes> record : records)".     -->
    <!-- "record" is a restricted, not a reserved, identifier: this is legal     -->
    <!-- Java 21 and it is the naming used throughout the Kafka client docs.     -->
    <sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s6213.ruleKey>java:S6213</sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s6213.ruleKey>
    <sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s6213.resourceKey>**/*.java</sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s6213.resourceKey>

    <!-- S3077: volatile is not enough for a non thread safe type. Scoped to     -->
    <!-- FMod_DatasetAvailabilityFilter, where both fields hold immutable        -->
    <!-- Set.copyOf / Map.copyOf values that are only ever replaced wholesale,   -->
    <!-- so a volatile reference is precisely the right idiom. The rule looks at -->
    <!-- the declared type, not the usage. NOT suppressed elsewhere: the other   -->
    <!-- four occurrences (volatile ObjectNode shared between job and servlet    -->
    <!-- threads) are genuine and remain open.                                  -->
    <sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s3077filter.ruleKey>java:S3077</sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s3077filter.ruleKey>
    <sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s3077filter.resourceKey>**/FMod_DatasetAvailabilityFilter.java</sonar.issue.ignore.multicriteria.s3077filter.resourceKey>

    <!-- S5786: redundant public modifiers on JUnit 5 tests. Jupiter does not    -->
